Minato's patch to frameworks/base's media/java/android/media/audiofx/AudioEffect.java at android-15.0.0_r1 (Apache-2.0),
the audio effects plan: the static initializer loads no libaudioeffect_jni, and the setup passes no attribution source.

Why: AudioEffect's ten natives are libandroid_runtime's (framework/native/android_runtime/android_media_AudioEffect.cpp,
the local effect service), registered when the process starts, as MediaCodec's are (mediacodec-without-media-jni.patch).
The attribution source is a parcel of the calling app's identity for the audio server's permission check; Minato has no
audio server, so the natives get null.

--- a/media/java/android/media/audiofx/AudioEffect.java
+++ b/media/java/android/media/audiofx/AudioEffect.java
@@ -74,7 +74,7 @@
 
 public class AudioEffect {
     static {
-        System.loadLibrary("audioeffect_jni");
+        // Minato: the natives are libandroid_runtime's (android_media_AudioEffect.cpp), registered at the start.
         native_init();
     }
 
@@ -522,13 +522,9 @@
 
         // native initialization
         // TODO b/182469354: Make consistent with AudioRecord
-        int initResult;
-        try (ScopedParcelState attributionSourceState =  AttributionSource.myAttributionSource()
-                .asScopedParcelState()) {
-            initResult = native_setup(new WeakReference<>(this), type.toString(), uuid.toString(),
-                    priority, audioSession, deviceType, deviceAddress, id, desc,
-                    attributionSourceState.getParcel(), probe);
-        }
+        // Minato: no attribution source reaches the natives, which are the local effect service's.
+        int initResult = native_setup(new WeakReference<>(this), type.toString(), uuid.toString(),
+                priority, audioSession, deviceType, deviceAddress, id, desc, null, probe);
         if (initResult != SUCCESS && initResult != ALREADY_EXISTS) {
             Log.e(TAG, "Error code " + initResult
                     + " when initializing AudioEffect.");
